Thanks a lot, Bill.

88
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,520
Thank you, Clark.

89
00:05:55,520 --> 00:06:00,440
In this podcast coming up, I have a discussion that I recorded this week with a friend

90
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:04,280
of mine who is a member of Scouts Canada.

91
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:08,600
One thing I think would be useful if this change comes to pass and we have a new membership

92
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:14,880
policy, is to look at how other Scouting organizations have handled it and what they've been doing.

93
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:20,280
So I asked Dean to join me here on the podcast to talk a little bit about those issues.

94
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:23,880
So after we talk to Dean, we've also got a couple of emails to answer, and that's

95
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:26,800
going to take care of the rest of this podcast.

96
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:45,840
So let's get started, shall we?

97
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:53,080
So joining me is Dean Post and Dean, a Scouter Dean, as he is better known in the Interwebs,

98
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:57,120
is a friend of the podcast and we've had him on before,

99
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:01,880
And Dean is up there in Canada where he is a venture advisor.

100
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,120
How are you this evening, Dean?

101
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,120
I'm very well, Clark,

102
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,120
Thank you,

103
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,200
But we're just being hit by a storm coming out from the US.

104
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,800
What are you guys sending us?

105
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:12,880
I believe it's snow.

106
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:17,840
We don't like snow very much down here, and so we're trying to send as much north

107
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:18,840
as possible.

108
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:22,240
Well, it's well time, because we're headed off on a small snowshoe trip this week

109
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:24,360
and a large one next weekend. so thank you,

110
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,360
We appreciate it.

111
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:32,600
One of the perennial concerns that I have had come up, Dean, is that there seems

112
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:36,560
to be a correspondence at the time when Scouts Canada stopped banning people

113
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:41,800
from membership based on sexual orientation and some kind of tremendous drop

114
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,040
in membership numbers.

115
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,440
Do you make that association?

116
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:44,960
No, though,

117
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:47,240
That's complete misconception.

118
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,960
Scouts Canada did have declining numbers.

119
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,680
Since the late 70s we've had declining numbers

120
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:57,240
And because of alternate choices for youth- they can do many different things

121
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:59,480
that didn't need to be able to

122
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:02,720
And the fact that our population growth slowed down.

123
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:06,680
We just didn't have that kind of continued growth in our population.

124
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:08,240
therefore the decreased growth in scouting-

125
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,840
So that was continuous growth-

126
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:13,440
That did not happen in 1998 or whatever date you want to peg,

127
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:16,040
when we became fully inclusive.

128
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:18,640
We did not have significant decrease because of that.

129
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:19,640
That's a misnomer.

130
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:24,280
Is it accurate to say that since 1998, membership in Scouts Canada has

131
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,000
dropped by 50%?

132
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:34,319
So in about 1998, we had just shy of 200,000 members.

133
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:36,600
We're now at about 100,000 members.

134
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:37,280
So you're right,

135
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:41,039
We've had about a 50% decrease since 1998..

136
00:08:41,039 --> 00:08:45,840
But that is an ongoing decrease. that's been happening since 1981.

137
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:48,840
So that was just a natural progression.

138
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:51,920
But again, as I stated, where our membership has stopped

139
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,040
that decline and now we're starting to grow again.

140
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:58,640
Since 2009,. we've been in a growth status for the last few years.

141
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,640
And what do you owe that growth to do? you think

142
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:04,440
It's a growth because we are modernizing Scouts Canada.

143
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:07,480
We have reinvigorated our programs.

144
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:09,800
We've listened more to what the youth want

145
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,040
and tried to make the youth more of the drivers

146
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,320
of the organization, just like Bayton, Powell and Vision,

147
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:17,560
where it was a movement where the youth caused a direction.

148
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,320
We've gone back to that roots but modernized

149
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:23,440
and gave them the power to set direction.

150
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,640
They have true power across Scouts Canada,

151
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:29,200
everywhere, from a national youth commissioner down

152
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,320
to group youth commissioners who help drive the program,

153
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:35,040
make sure it's relevant to today's youth,

154
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:37,360
while sticking to our core of outdoor activities.

155
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,560
I've seen some things about that

156
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:44,400
And there's actually kind of a corollary youth

157
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:49,000
executive structure. that's kind of- I guess,

158
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,079
if I was to borrow a term- vertically integrated

159
00:09:52,079 --> 00:09:56,120
Opinions and their ideas actually make it

160
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:59,280
to the people who actually call it

161
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:03,600
right policy and program and things.

162
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,120
Currently, for example, Scouts Canada

163
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:07,240
is going through a major program review

164
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:10,480
with a revitalization coming out next year or two,

165
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:13,680
And each one of these teams beavers through Rovers.

166
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:15,360
there are youth sitting around the table

167
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,320
and giving their input as equals

168
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,720
and helping us set these directions

169
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:21,000
so that it's fun and exciting

170
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,520
and based on their needs and wants.

171
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:27,520
And were you involved at 98

172
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,320
when this policy change was made?

173
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,120
Yeah, I was, and I didn't notice

174
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:37,240
What was the. I imagine there were some talk.

175
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:39,200
What were people talking about at the time?

176
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:42,240
Frankly, I don't remember any talk about inclusiveness

177
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:46,480
As far as I knew. I joined, I started at 91 as a leader

178
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:50,000
And in the early or the mid 90s

179
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,600
there was talk of becoming co-ed

180
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:56,200
And I know that was causing some ruffled feathers

181
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:58,920
And I don't remember Scouts telling me they would go,

182
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:01,000
they'd quit the moment to go co-ed

183
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,560
And I can tell you- I can think of several of them

184
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,720
who are still involved-

185
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:07,000
So they didn't quit and they saw the advantage of it.

186
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,360
When the late 90s came,

187
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:12,000
when this inclusive thing happened, I didn't even notice.

188
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:16,040
So it was just all part of our society's evolution

189
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,880
And I didn't notice. Scouts can

190
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:21,560
and I'd never heard anyone speak against the concept at all

191
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,400
or be concerned about it.

192
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:26,600
Have you had occasion to be at different events

193
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,200
and things like that with American Scouts?

194
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:32,520
Yes, we go to an international camp every year,

195
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:36,800
which is at least 50% Scouts from the US.

196
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,840
They're present. plus, I've been to World Jamboree,

197
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:41,720
where US Scouts and Scouts from around the world are there.

198
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:43,360
So I've had plenty of opportunity to interact

199
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,400
with my brothers from the BSA.

200
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:49,080
And has there been any concerns expressed

201
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:51,840
over the fact that you're an inclusive organization

202
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:52,880
at those events?

203
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:53,720
Not that I noticed.

204
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:56,080
I know years, a few years back,

205
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:58,240
when we started having more and more girls,

206
00:11:58,240 --> 00:11:59,960
you'd be sitting around having coffee

207
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:02,040
with the US Scouts and they'd go.

208
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,640
they'd comment that gee, you guys have girls,

209
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,200
How many girls have you to have a discussion?

210
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:08,440
And they'd make comment that, gee,

211
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,360
it just seems like normal here.

212
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,560
Yeah,

213
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,240
And as far as inclusiveness, no,

214
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:14,400
no one's ever raised the issue.

215
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,920
I mean no

216
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:18,400
One of the concerns that I'm hearing raised

217
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:22,560
is that if we were to open membership,

218
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:25,360
that this would cause no end of difficulty

219
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:29,680
with the danger of sexual activity or sexual attraction

220
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:32,520
between boys on camp outs

221
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,360
and sleeping in the same tent

222
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,280
or using the same facilities.

223
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:40,120
Has that been an issue for Scouts Canada?

224
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,720
No, we've not had that issue,

225
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,640
Never even considered the fact of people

226
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:46,440
who maybe attract to the same sex

227
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,320
and sleep in the same tents.

228
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:49,800
I mean, we have similar policies to the BSA

229
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:50,840
and the fact that you know,

230
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:52,400
for example, with our senior members,

231
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,320
we have what we call the sad rule-

232
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,760
no sex, alcohol or drugs-

233
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,360
and they seem to understand that

234
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,640
Sexuality is not really a big question.

235
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:01,960
I mean, the kids are kids.

236
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,800
they're out having great times.

237
00:13:03,800 --> 00:13:06,600
As far as same sex sharing quarters,

238
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:08,160
we've never- I've never- come across

239
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,640
that sort of situation. what's been an issue,

240
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:13,439
Even in your own military, for example,

241
00:13:13,439 --> 00:13:16,079
which has now gone fully inclusive.

242
00:13:16,079 --> 00:13:17,439
they haven't made changes.

243
00:13:17,439 --> 00:13:19,439
They don't have separate dressing rooms

244
00:13:19,439 --> 00:13:21,839
or showers based on your sexuality.

245
00:13:21,839 --> 00:13:24,000
It's just being inclusive society.

246
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,600
If there was some kind of real problem

247
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:30,240
or real concern over any of these things

248
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,240
that we've been talking about,

249
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:34,160
that, it would be a topic of discussion

250
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:36,839
and possibly training and things like that.

251
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:39,840
but you're so I'm pushing you around a little bit.

252
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:42,040
You're for real. you're telling me

253
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:43,940
that that is just a non-issue.

254
00:13:45,080 --> 00:13:46,320
I have not encountered it.

255
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:49,960
We do talk about sexuality when we're being trained.

256
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,440
We deal with the co-ed situation.

257
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,080
Sexuality is something we talk about

258
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,760
in training and wood badge

259
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,200
and being accepting of kids,

260
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,080
especially in the teen years,

261
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:02,840
and but trying to give them a healthy lifestyle

262
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,720
and give them alternatives to perhaps

263
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:07,240
listen to their physicalness while at camp.

264
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:10,320
Guys have gone through some big changes of late.

265
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:14,040
You're characterizing these changes as pretty positive.

266
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:16,920
Has there been no backlash, hard feelings

267
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,560
about some of these things that have changed

268
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,560
in Scouts Canada?

269
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:24,120
In my experience, I've not heard of anyone being upset

270
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:27,760
or quitting or threatening to. you know,

271
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:31,160
pull sponsorship due to our inclusive nature.

272
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:34,240
But, quite frankly, when they started talking

273
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:35,760
about selling our scout camps,

274
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:38,680
that created more fervor than being inclusive.

275
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:42,360
As councils merge and things happen,

276
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:44,280
sometimes properties have to be let go,

277
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,440
and that's a pretty emotional thing.

278
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:48,360
Exactly, and that becomes more emotional

279
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:50,000
than this discussion.

280
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,600
We have different sponsoring institutions,

281
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:57,360
and these may be churches or civic groups of some kind.

282
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:59,880
They make all the decisions

283
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:02,920
as far as who is a suitable leader,

284
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:06,120
Whatever description. that is issued by the BSA

285
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,960
as being the minimal standard,

286
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,720
but some people go over and above that.

287
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:11,800
Is that common in Canada?

288
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:15,280
Yeah, well, in a way, we still have sponsors

289
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:17,720
or partners, just like you do.

290
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,200
Many of them are community groups.

291
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:22,080
In some cases, they are religious organizations.

292
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,920
Our affiliation with religious organizations

293
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:25,240
are a lower percentage.

294
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:29,040
So, having said that, yes, there are cases

295
00:15:29,079 --> 00:15:32,800
where they might be sponsored

296
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,280
by a particular religious organization.

297
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:38,000
They do have various guidelines that you must be part of,

298
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,760
where you have to be part of that church community,

299
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:43,599
for example, to be a member of that group.

300
00:15:43,599 --> 00:15:48,240
That does still occur, yes, but it's much lower,

301
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,839
and community groups and schools

302
00:15:49,839 --> 00:15:52,400
are the biggest part of our sponsors here.

303
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,079
Would you like to talk to a 17-year-old

304
00:15:54,079 --> 00:15:55,520
about these views,

305
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:57,000
Because actually my son is working away

306
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,480
in the kitchen here.

307
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,040
Let's listen to what I say.

308
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:03,000
He wants to put in his sense.

309
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,760
Okay, well, we'll put him on then.

310
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:06,240
His name is Alex,

311
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:08,840
So he's 17,. he's a venture scout.

312
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:12,480
And Alex, this is Scott or Clark Green.

313
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,040
Hello there,

314
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:15,880
Hey, Alex, how are you

315
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,440
Not too bad yourself?

316
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:19,760
So how long have you been involved with Scouts?

317
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:21,560
I'm on my 13th year right now.

318
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:26,000
I'm talking to your dad about some of the things

319
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,760
that are happening in the BSA right now

320
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,000
And, as you're probably aware,

321
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,880
that we're contemplating a change

322
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:35,280
to our membership standards that would allow people

323
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:37,640
that would remove the bearer we've had

324
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:41,320
to people of different sexual orientations-

325
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:43,000
Yes, I have been following that.

326
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,160
You have any thoughts about that.

327
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,040
Well, I've actually experienced people

328
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:50,720
with all sorts of sexual orientations out of camp.

329
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:53,400
I've seen people with different opinions on it all,

330
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:55,640
but it's never become an issue.

331
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,240
Potentially like people who are gay

332
00:16:57,240 --> 00:17:00,400
that do sleep in the tent with other males, for instance,

333
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:03,520
And I've talked to them and it's never been an issue

334
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:08,240
They all understand and that they just

335
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,359
they don't care about. it is.

336
00:17:09,359 --> 00:17:11,639
I think the most important thing is

337
00:17:11,639 --> 00:17:14,920
part about inclusiveness is that they're treated fairly

338
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,480
and they're treated the same,

339
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:19,040
And just because of somebody's sexual orientation,

340
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,879
that doesn't mean that we need to completely exclude them

341
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:24,000
in the sense of having a separate sleeping area.

342
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,960
So everybody's under that same understanding

343
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,360
and they all seem to be very good about it here.

344
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:30,840
So the world outside of scouting

345
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,240
and the world in scouting

346
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:33,840
people generally understand this.

347
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:35,400
All right,

348
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,440
You're quite a bit younger than I am.

349
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:40,520
My son's probably about 10 years older than you.

350
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:45,520
There are a lot of scouters my age and around my age

351
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:50,560
who are feeling as if this is going to cause us

352
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:52,040
a great deal of trouble.

353
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:53,320
Is this something that your age group

354
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,760
is thinking about all the time

355
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:59,280
And is this just something that is just the way things are?

356
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:00,120
Well, yeah,

357
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:00,960
I think you have a very good point there

358
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,399
of being the way things are,

359
00:18:02,399 --> 00:18:05,399
but definitely it is something that's become more and more

360
00:18:05,399 --> 00:18:06,240
aware.

361
00:18:06,240 --> 00:18:08,919
It's something that's openly talked about. in that sense.

362
00:18:08,919 --> 00:18:09,760
Yeah,

363
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:11,600
It has just kind of become like the social norm

364
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:14,200
that it's accepted, it's talked about

365
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:16,200
And people have their opinions on it all,

366
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,360
but generally it seems accepted.

367
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:21,280
And you're saying about how some of the older scouters

368
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,400
are maybe a little scared about it,

369
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,320
And that's perfectly fair.

370
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:27,360
Change is always scary.

371
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:31,200
Even as a 17-year-old, things have changed.

372
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:34,200
It can be scary and there are doubts,

373
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,960
there are hesitations.

374
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:40,960
but when you're moving forward in trying to do what's right

375
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:43,720
and trying to be all-inclusive,

376
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,760
that change can still be scary.

377
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,720
but you can also hold true to yourself

378
00:18:47,720 --> 00:18:49,400
that you're doing it for the right reasons

379
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,600
and you're doing the right thing.

380
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:52,160
That's good advice, Alex.

381
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:54,920
I hope people can accept that.

382
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:58,600
Tell me a little bit about the more recent innovations

383
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:03,000
in Scouts Canada so far as the youth are involved.

384
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,480
Your dad was kind of going over that with me a bit.

385
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:08,080
Have you participated in any of those things?

386
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:09,120
Oh, definitely.

387
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:11,480
A little while ago I took my focus training,

388
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:14,840
which is a leadership training run by youth

389
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:16,800
here in Scouts Canada.

390
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,480
So I took that training a couple of years ago.

391
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:20,480
and one thing that they did introduce then,

392
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:22,720
which was the first time for myself, it did exist before

393
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:26,280
but it was the ladder of leadership

394
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:29,520
And it's all about, I believe, seven or eight stages

395
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:34,399
on how youth are involved and based on the leadership

396
00:19:34,399 --> 00:19:35,720
that they have, in the leadership

397
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:39,200
that their scouters or advisors and ventures have.

398
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:41,520
So there's different steps and it's all about

399
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:45,000
what step are you at and can you achieve a higher level?

400
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,280
And, looking at it,

401
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:49,600
our group at the time was actually quite high.

402
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,200
Now I am working with my group youth commissioner,

403
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,960
who's also a great friend of mine,

404
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:55,000
and we're trying to encourage,

405
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,600
especially within our group,

406
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:58,680
to have a large amount of youth participation,

407
00:19:58,680 --> 00:20:03,120
encouraging the senior scouts to really step ahead

408
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:06,160
and try and teach the younger scouts.

409
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:09,080
So, yes, it has been a little difficult

410
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:11,960
and with the revitalization of the program,

411
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:14,720
but everybody seems to be doing their best

412
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:16,360
to push it forward

413
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:20,880
And with time I think it can be very well accomplished

414
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:23,080
and I definitely am looking forward

415
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,960
to everything that's happening.

416
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:26,160
Well, thank you so much.

417
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,000
I appreciate it.

418
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,240
Is there anything else you'd like to add?

419
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,480
Just that, all the way through scouting,

420
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,280
I've loved what I do.

421
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:35,520
It's become not only a family thing

422
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:37,680
that I do with my father and my brother,

423
00:20:37,680 --> 00:20:40,560
but scouting itself has become my family.

424
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:42,720
Yeah, I think we all feel that way at one point.

425
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,840
So thanks again, Alex,

426
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:45,680
I really appreciate it.

427
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,720
Nice talking to you,

428
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,080
Nice to talk to you.

429
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,280
So if you had buttons on your vest

430
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:51,960
before I started talking to the boy,

431
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:54,080
you should not have any now, right,

432
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,920
That's true. that's true.

433
00:20:56,920 --> 00:20:57,960
Yes,

434
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,320
Yeah, what a great guy.

435
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:00,160
Yes,

436
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:02,280
Well, listen, I really appreciate you taking the time

437
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:03,400
to talk to me again,

438
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:05,520
Hey, Eric Clark, and keep up the good work.

439
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:06,880
Thank you so much.

440
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,720
All right, good talk to you.

441
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:13,560
Give me a letter, send it by name,

442
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,880
Email, that is, folks.

443
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:18,480
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

444
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:30,360
Dave sent me an email and he asked this question.

445
00:21:30,360 --> 00:21:33,160
We had a debate in our troop about whether or not

446
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:37,320
scouts are to be held to a higher standard than others.

447
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:39,040
Well, I think this is true.

448
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:41,760
I also know that scouts are boys

449
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:43,520
and they're still learning and growing.

450
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:45,919
Dave, that's an interesting question

451
00:21:45,919 --> 00:21:49,600
And we are dedicated to being held to a higher standard.

452
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:51,879
We have the scout oath and law as a standard.

453
00:21:51,879 --> 00:21:56,040
But just to say that we hold scouts to a higher standard,

454
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:58,520
I think, is only half the story.

455
00:21:58,520 --> 00:22:00,439
I'm focused on scouts developing

456
00:22:00,439 --> 00:22:03,399
an internal standard of morals and ethics,

457
00:22:03,399 --> 00:22:05,800
not imposing a standard on them.

458
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:08,000
The oath and the law aren't, to my mind,

459
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,720
standards of measurement.

460
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:10,879
They're aspirations.

461
00:22:10,879 --> 00:22:13,080
If we're measured against the scout oath and law,

462
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:15,639
we're all going to be lacking in one way or another.

463
00:22:15,639 --> 00:22:17,240
We're always going to come up short

464
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:19,639
and that's never all that encouraging.

465
00:22:19,639 --> 00:22:22,399
If we look at the ideals of the oath and law

466
00:22:22,399 --> 00:22:25,480
as aspirations, something to journey towards,

467
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:28,159
we can mark our progress along the way.

468
00:22:28,159 --> 00:22:30,120
Now, that may be a form of measurement,

469
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:33,320
but it's different than being held to a higher standard.

470
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:36,040
It's advancing to a destination.

471
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:39,240
We don't mark our progress in miles yet to travel,

472
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:41,320
but in the number that we have crossed,

473
00:22:41,320 --> 00:22:43,240
and that's always a positive number

474
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,800
and it keeps getting bigger,

475
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:46,600
And I think there's a difference there.

476
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,280
Instead of looking at what we lack,

477
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,960
we look at what we've gained.

478
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:51,520
It may seem a fine distinction,

479
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:54,520
but I think it's important when we're working with scouts.

480
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:58,800
Nobody else gets to measure our progress as individuals

481
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:01,439
because nobody else knows us well enough.

482
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:05,520
We'd look within, see where we started and where we are,

483
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:07,360
and we judge for ourselves.

484
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:08,560
Nobody else gets to judge

485
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,760
because nobody's reached the 100% mark

486
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:13,440
in any point of the scout oath and law.

487
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:17,240
So the practical application of this idea in scouting

488
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:20,920
is calling on the developing internal standard

489
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:25,420
in each scout and asking him how he judges himself.

490
00:23:25,420 --> 00:23:26,740
Did he do his best?

491
00:23:26,740 --> 00:23:28,960
Can he honestly say that he's progressed

492
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,600
in his expectations?

493
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:34,880
Developing the capacity to be honest with ourselves,

494
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:38,020
to learn to internalize the higher and better standards,

495
00:23:38,020 --> 00:23:40,120
is very important work.

496
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:43,760
In other words, there's only one standard and one judge,

497
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:46,280
the one that we have in our hearts and minds.

498
00:23:46,280 --> 00:23:48,880
When a boy is faced with a difficult situation

499
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:52,160
or decision, we want him to have a solid, moral

500
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:55,920
and ethical internal standard to call on.

501
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:59,080
We build that capacity by collaborating with it,

502
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:01,760
by asking questions and getting a boy to learn

503
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:04,760
and listen to that standard to find the answers.

504
00:24:04,760 --> 00:24:07,440
Now, in our judgment, some boys behave better than others.

505
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:09,560
but what about their own judgment?

506
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:12,720
The quiet, attentive boy at your meeting:

507
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:16,600
he may be calling on about 3% of his capacities

508
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:19,440
to be able to be quiet and attentive.

509
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:21,840
The noisy, distracted boy at your meeting

510
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:25,480
may be calling on 110% of his capacity.

511
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:28,720
If we hold them both to the same external standard,

512
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,580
I think we miss the point.

513
00:24:30,580 --> 00:24:33,440
It's easy to create normative behavior in scouts.

514
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:36,400
I can do it in seconds by just raising my voice

515
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,860
and looming. you know what I'm talking about.

516
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:44,700
But I'm not so much interested in normative behavior

517
00:24:44,700 --> 00:24:48,280
as I am in. what's going on inside?

518
00:24:48,280 --> 00:24:51,400
Is the boy striving towards becoming a better person?

519
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:53,880
Is he internalizing the morals and ethics

520
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:57,400
that will serve him and everyone he comes in contact to

521
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:58,920
for the rest of his life?

522
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:01,520
And I think to find that out we need to talk with him,

523
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:03,700
We need to ask him those questions.

524
00:25:03,700 --> 00:25:07,600
And finally, I'll add that I'm in no way suggesting

525
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,760
that, if we look at the scout, oath and law

526
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:13,100
not as an external standard but as an aspiration,

527
00:25:13,100 --> 00:25:16,680
that that consciences bad behavior. not at all.

528
00:25:16,680 --> 00:25:19,120
What I am saying is that our work

529
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:21,120
and the aim of what we're doing

530
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:24,640
is to take that ethical and moral standard

531
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:27,160
and to help boys internalize it

532
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:30,560
so that they can call on it when the decisions of life

533
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:32,600
come along that they need to make.

534
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:36,800
Jeff Zook writes from Oxnard, California, Troupe 222.

535
00:25:36,800 --> 00:25:37,960
And he says: thank you very much

536
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:39,720
for the great information found on your blog.

537
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:41,600
I'm a subscriber and a scouter

538
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:43,480
and therefore I'm always learning.

539
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:45,920
My question is about the troop meeting plan.

540
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:48,660
We have a mid-sized troop of about 35 boys

541
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:50,320
and we encourage the patrol method.

542
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:51,960
I am having difficulty, though,

543
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:53,480
in getting the senior patrol leader

544
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:55,240
to send out the troop meeting plan

545
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:57,340
to his patrol leaders early enough in the week

546
00:25:57,340 --> 00:26:00,080
so that they know what's happening and what to plan for.

547
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:02,960
We even have a brief meeting with the patrol leaders

548
00:26:02,960 --> 00:26:04,040
and the senior patrol leader

549
00:26:04,040 --> 00:26:06,679
after every meeting to discuss next week's plans,

550
00:26:06,679 --> 00:26:08,480
And I quietly put the emphasis

551
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:11,659
on getting the troop meeting plan out early.

552
00:26:11,659 --> 00:26:14,760
This suggestion has been offered by me many times.

553
00:26:14,760 --> 00:26:16,580
The result is usually a troop meeting plan

554
00:26:16,580 --> 00:26:17,879
being sent out the night before

555
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:20,600
or sometimes the day of the troop meeting.

556
00:26:20,600 --> 00:26:22,960
Any suggestions offered to help our scouts understand

557
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:25,160
the importance of that kind of planning

558
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:27,160
and getting everybody to understand

559
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:29,040
and know what's being planned?

560
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:31,320
Well, first of all, thank you, Jeff, for being in touch

561
00:26:31,320 --> 00:26:32,920
and thanks for the kind words there.

562
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:37,640
I think that this whole idea of planning

563
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:41,080
and preparation and getting meetings off the ground

564
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:43,080
and boys doing it is something

565
00:26:43,080 --> 00:26:44,800
that I hear about time and time again,

566
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:47,200
So it's not just you.

567
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:50,480
This is something that we really need to work at

568
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:51,400
as scout leaders.

569
00:26:51,400 --> 00:26:53,120
A lot of times it's our whole job

570
00:26:53,120 --> 00:26:55,760
in working with and training the youth leaders

571
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:58,360
to be able to make these things happen,

572
00:26:58,360 --> 00:27:00,560
And I've come to look at it like this:

573
00:27:00,560 --> 00:27:02,400
Think of four things.

574
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:07,320
Think of planning, preparation, structure and content.

575
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:10,840
Now, planning is something that we talk about a lot,

576
00:27:10,840 --> 00:27:12,120
And I think we talk about it

577
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:14,640
to the point where we overemphasize it.

578
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:16,680
Planning is really two things.

579
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:18,480
Let's just break it down.

580
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:22,520
It's deciding what to do and who's going to do it,

581
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:25,720
And there's a few other associated logistical things

582
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:27,600
in there, like what do I need to do it

583
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:28,920
and where are we going to do it,

584
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:33,200
But simply it's what to do and who's going to do it.

585
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:36,280
That's a process that takes a few minutes at the most.

586
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:38,760
Preparation is something we don't talk about as much

587
00:27:38,760 --> 00:27:40,800
because we kind of think it's part of planning

588
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,320
and leave it at that.

589
00:27:42,320 --> 00:27:44,680
I'm starting to work with my patrol leaders counsel

590
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:47,080
to separate these two things out.

591
00:27:47,080 --> 00:27:50,200
Instead of a 45 minute meeting around a table

592
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:53,160
where they're quote, unquote- planning,

593
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:55,320
how about if they spend about 10 minutes

594
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:58,840
planning and the rest of the time preparing?

595
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:01,040
This means getting up from that table

596
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:02,720
and putting your hands on the materials

597
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:04,280
and the gear and whatever you need

598
00:28:04,280 --> 00:28:07,160
to work out the way your meeting's going to work

599
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:10,400
and then getting with it and starting to prepare-

600
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:12,200
actually prepare for that.

601
00:28:12,200 --> 00:28:14,500
I think what we've understood in the past

602
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:16,580
is that the patrol leaders, counsel

603
00:28:16,580 --> 00:28:18,580
would get together and plan

604
00:28:18,580 --> 00:28:20,540
and then the scouts with responsibilities

605
00:28:20,540 --> 00:28:23,620
at the next meeting would prepare on their own time

606
00:28:23,620 --> 00:28:25,540
and just kind of do that individually.

607
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:28,620
and hey, you know, sometimes it would happen,

608
00:28:28,620 --> 00:28:31,180
but most of the time they would remember

609
00:28:31,180 --> 00:28:33,340
maybe 10 minutes before they got to the meeting

610
00:28:33,340 --> 00:28:35,060
or maybe after they got to the meeting

611
00:28:35,060 --> 00:28:37,060
and the senior patrol, everybody reminded them.

612
00:28:37,060 --> 00:28:39,260
even if the senior patrol leaders done his job

613
00:28:39,260 --> 00:28:41,260
and called them and things.

614
00:28:41,300 --> 00:28:45,860
the preparation step just doesn't happen a lot of the time.

615
00:28:45,860 --> 00:28:47,900
So to focus on that,

616
00:28:47,900 --> 00:28:49,980
perhaps the thing we ought to do

617
00:28:49,980 --> 00:28:54,180
is introduce the idea that planning and preparation

618
00:28:54,180 --> 00:28:55,860
are two separate steps

619
00:28:55,860 --> 00:28:58,620
and then make sure that they have time

620
00:28:58,620 --> 00:29:02,780
to work on the preparation part of their plans.

621
00:29:02,780 --> 00:29:05,300
The two other terms that we introduced:

622
00:29:05,300 --> 00:29:06,940
the first was structure.

623
00:29:06,940 --> 00:29:08,900
This is kind of like the schedule,

624
00:29:08,900 --> 00:29:11,460
the framework of a meeting or an outing

625
00:29:11,460 --> 00:29:14,380
What's going to happen and when it's going to happen.

626
00:29:14,380 --> 00:29:17,580
This is usually a fairly set structure

627
00:29:17,580 --> 00:29:19,220
and it's not something that

628
00:29:19,220 --> 00:29:21,900
the patrol leaders counsel has to invent.

629
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:24,660
It's basically the same schedule for every meeting.

630
00:29:24,660 --> 00:29:27,740
So if they don't have to invent a structure,

631
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:32,220
they can pay more attention to the content

632
00:29:32,220 --> 00:29:33,220
of what they're doing,

633
00:29:33,220 --> 00:29:35,060
And content I guess we could describe

634
00:29:35,060 --> 00:29:36,540
as just the actual things they're doing,

635
00:29:36,540 --> 00:29:38,220
you know, tying knots or packing packs

636
00:29:38,220 --> 00:29:40,060
or cooking or hiking or whatever.

637
00:29:40,060 --> 00:29:43,140
What many of us are asking our patrol leaders counsel to do

638
00:29:43,140 --> 00:29:44,980
is to start with a blank sheet

639
00:29:44,980 --> 00:29:47,500
and to invent the structure and the content

640
00:29:47,500 --> 00:29:49,260
and then to develop a plan,

641
00:29:49,260 --> 00:29:51,580
And we almost never talk about preparing.

642
00:29:51,580 --> 00:29:54,300
Inventing structures and content

643
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:56,620
is kind of heavy lifting for scouts.

644
00:29:56,620 --> 00:29:59,220
That's the point where they are staring at each other

645
00:29:59,220 --> 00:30:01,860
across the table and wondering what to do.

646
00:30:01,860 --> 00:30:05,380
The program gives them most of the structure that they need

647
00:30:05,380 --> 00:30:08,380
and gives them most of the content that they need.

648
00:30:08,380 --> 00:30:10,700
Now, if they want to invent something,

649
00:30:10,700 --> 00:30:12,020
certainly they can.

650
00:30:12,020 --> 00:30:15,860
But instead of having to do that all the time,

651
00:30:15,860 --> 00:30:20,220
they can choose to use that existing content and structure.

652
00:30:20,220 --> 00:30:24,100
In fact, they will use existing content and structure

653
00:30:24,100 --> 00:30:28,460
a lot of the time because that's what scouts do

654
00:30:28,460 --> 00:30:31,380
And most of it's already set up and ready to go.

655
00:30:31,380 --> 00:30:33,020
It's all in the handbook.

656
00:30:33,020 --> 00:30:35,020
So maybe the answer to your question, Jeff,

657
00:30:35,020 --> 00:30:37,780
is to stop thinking about plans and structure

658
00:30:37,780 --> 00:30:40,260
and content so much and start thinking more

659
00:30:40,260 --> 00:30:41,780
about preparation.

660
00:30:41,780 --> 00:30:43,500
We start with this framework,

661
00:30:43,500 --> 00:30:45,740
the big schedule of trips and meetings.

662
00:30:45,740 --> 00:30:48,020
We see the content that fits into that.

663
00:30:48,020 --> 00:30:50,980
We plan by making sure that everybody has a role

664
00:30:50,980 --> 00:30:54,379
and we spend the lion's share of the time preparing

665
00:30:54,379 --> 00:30:56,820
rather than concerning ourselves with the other things.

666
00:30:56,820 --> 00:31:00,300
So when your patrol leaders, counsel is working together,

667
00:31:00,300 --> 00:31:02,580
let's make a clear division between

668
00:31:02,580 --> 00:31:03,940
all four of those things-

669
00:31:04,020 --> 00:31:05,660
the structure, the content,

670
00:31:05,660 --> 00:31:07,460
the planning and the preparation-

671
00:31:07,460 --> 00:31:09,380
and think about really capitalizing

672
00:31:09,380 --> 00:31:11,500
and focusing on the preparation piece,

673
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:14,700
because I think that's the part that is often missing

674
00:31:14,700 --> 00:31:16,820
and it's assumed that it's just part of planning,

675
00:31:16,820 --> 00:31:19,020
but I don't think scouts assume that.

676
00:31:19,020 --> 00:31:21,300
I think it's helpful for us to create an environment

677
00:31:21,300 --> 00:31:23,420
where they can not only plan

678
00:31:23,420 --> 00:31:24,780
but they can prepare.

679
00:31:24,780 --> 00:31:25,620
Okay,

680
00:31:51,740 --> 00:31:53,780
Well, thank you so much for listening to this edition

681
00:31:53,820 --> 00:31:55,580
of the Scoutmaster podcast.

